{"id":"mahabharata-4-038","work":"mahabharata","part":4,"partName":"विराटपर्व","partNameEn":"Virata Parva","unit":38,"title":"अष्टात्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 38 · The weapons in the shami tree","summary":{"en":"At the shami tree Arjuna tells Uttara to climb up and bring down the Pandavas' weapons. Uttara, afraid of the corpse, obeys, and is amazed by the splendid bows, quivers and swords; Arjuna tells him which belongs to each of the brothers, beginning with his own Gandiva.","kn":"ಶಮೀವೃಕ್ಷದ ಬಳಿ ಮೇಲೇರಿ ಪಾಂಡವರ ಆಯುಧಗಳನ್ನು ಇಳಿಸೆಂದು ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಉತ್ತರನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಶವಕ್ಕೆ ಹೆದರಿದರೂ ಉತ್ತರನು ಆಜ್ಞೆ ಪಾಲಿಸಿ ಭವ್ಯ ಧನುಸ್ಸು, ಬತ್ತಳಿಕೆ, ಖಡ್ಗಗಳನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ಬೆರಗಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ತನ್ನ ಗಾಂಡೀವದಿಂದ ಆರಂಭಿಸಿ ಯಾವುದು ಯಾರದೆಂದು ಅರ್ಜುನನು ತಿಳಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"शमी वृक्ष के पास अर्जुन उत्तर से ऊपर चढ़कर पाण्डवों के शस्त्र उतारने को कहते हैं। शव से डरते हुए भी उत्तर आज्ञा मानता है और भव्य धनुषों, तरकशों और खड्गों को देखकर चकित होता है; अर्जुन अपने गाण्डीव से आरम्भ कर बताते हैं कि कौन-सा किस भाई का है।","te":"జమ్మిచెట్టు దగ్గర పైకెక్కి పాండవుల ఆయుధాలను దించమని అర్జునుడు ఉత్తరునికి చెబుతాడు. శవానికి భయపడినా ఉత్తరుడు ఆజ్ఞ పాటించి భవ్యమైన ధనుస్సులు, అమ్ములపొదులు, ఖడ్గాలను చూసి ఆశ్చర్యపోతాడు; తన గాండీవంతో మొదలుపెట్టి ఏది ఎవరిదో అర్జునుడు చెబుతాడు.","ta":"வன்னி மரத்தருகே மேலே ஏறிப் பாண்டவர்களின் ஆயுதங்களை இறக்குமாறு அர்ஜுனன் உத்தரனிடம் சொல்கிறான். பிணத்துக்கு அஞ்சினாலும் உத்தரன் கீழ்ப்படிந்து அற்புதமான வில்கள், அம்பறாத்தூணிகள், வாள்களைக் கண்டு வியக்க, தன் காண்டீவத்திலிருந்து தொடங்கி எது எந்தச் சகோதரனுடையது என்று அர்ஜுனன் சொல்கிறான்.","ml":"ശമിമരത്തിനരികെ, മുകളിൽ കയറി പാണ്ഡവരുടെ ആയുധങ്ങൾ താഴെയിറക്കാൻ അർജുനൻ ഉത്തരനോട് പറയുന്നു. ശവത്തെ ഭയന്ന ഉത്തരൻ അനുസരിക്കുന്നു; മനോഹരമായ വില്ലുകളും ആവനാഴികളും വാളുകളും കണ്ട് അവൻ അത്ഭുതപ്പെടുന്നു. ഓരോ സഹോദരന്റെയും ആയുധം ഏതാണെന്ന് അർജുനൻ പറഞ്ഞുകൊടുക്കുന്നു; തന്റെ സ്വന്തം ഗാണ്ഡീവത്തിൽനിന്നാണ് തുടക്കം."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 4.38; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Dec  1 2011","sections":[{"title":"गोग्रहणपर्व","titleEn":"Gograhana Parva (The cattle raid)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तां शमीमुपसंगम्य पार्थो वैराटिमब्रवीत् ।\nसुकुमारं समाज्ञातं संग्रामे नातिकोविदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the shami tree, Arjuna spoke to Virata's son, knowing him to be delicate and not very skilled in war."}},{"n":2,"text":"समादिष्टो मया क्षिप्रं धनूंष्यवहरोत्तर ।\nनेमानि हि त्वदीयानि सोढुं शक्ष्यन्ति मे बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Uttara, at my bidding quickly bring down the bows. Your own bows will not be able to bear my strength."}},{"n":3,"text":"भारं वापि गुरुं हर्तुं कुञ्जरं वा प्रमर्दितुम् ।\nमम वा बाहुविक्षेपं शत्रूनिह विजेष्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They could not carry a heavy burden or crush an elephant, nor withstand the sweep of my arms as I conquer enemies here."}},{"n":4,"text":"तस्माद्भूमिंजयारोह शमीमेतां पलाशिनीम् ।\nअस्यां हि पाण्डुपुत्राणां धनूंषि निहितान्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, Bhumimjaya, climb this leafy shami tree, for the bows of the sons of Pandu have been put away in it."}},{"n":5,"text":"युधिष्ठिरस्य भीमस्य बीभत्सोर्यमयोस्तथा ।\nध्वजाः शराश्च शूराणां दिव्यानि कवचानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"There are the bows of Yudhishthira, Bhima, Bibhatsu and the twins, along with the banners, arrows and divine armor of those heroes."}},{"n":6,"text":"अत्र चैतन्महावीर्यं धनुः पार्थस्य गाण्डिवम् ।\nएकं शतसहस्रेण संमितं राष्ट्रवर्धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And here is the great and mighty bow of Partha, the Gandiva, worth a hundred thousand bows, which makes a kingdom thrive."}},{"n":7,"text":"व्यायामसहमत्यर्थं तृणराजसमं महत् ।\nसर्वायुधमहामात्रं शत्रुसंबाधकारकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It can bear great strain, is huge like the king of grasses, is the foremost of all weapons, and is a torment to foes."}},{"n":8,"text":"सुवर्णविकृतं दिव्यं श्लक्ष्णमायतमव्रणम् ।\nअलं भारं गुरुं वोढुं दारुणं चारुदर्शनम् ।\nतादृशान्येव सर्वाणि बलवन्ति दृढानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Divine, adorned with gold, smooth, long and flawless, able to bear a heavy load, fearsome and lovely to look at; all the others are likewise strong and firm.\""}},{"text":"उत्तर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Uttara said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"अस्मिन्वृक्षे किलोद्बद्धं शरीरमिति नः श्रुतम् ।\nतदहं राजपुत्रः सन्स्पृशेयं पाणिना कथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We have heard that a corpse is tied up in this tree. How can I, a prince, touch it with my hand?"}},{"n":10,"text":"नैवंविधं मया युक्तमालब्धुं क्षत्रयोनिना ।\nमहता राजपुत्रेण मन्त्रयज्ञविदा सता ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is not fitting for me, born a Kshatriya, a great prince, a good man versed in mantras and sacrifice, to handle such a thing."}},{"n":11,"text":"स्पृष्टवन्तं शरीरं मां शववाहमिवाशुचिम् ।\nकथं वा व्यवहार्यं वै कुर्वीथास्त्वं बृहन्नडे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having touched a body, I would be unclean like one who carries a corpse. How would you let me do business with others afterward, Brihannada?\""}},{"text":"बृहन्नडोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brihannada said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"व्यवहार्यश्च राजेन्द्र शुचिश्चैव भविष्यसि ।\nधनूंष्येतानि मा भैस्त्वं शरीरं नात्र विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You will remain fit for dealings and pure, king among men. Do not fear these bows; there is no corpse here."}},{"n":13,"text":"दायादं मत्स्यराजस्य कुले जातं मनस्विनम् ।\nकथं त्वा निन्दितं कर्म कारयेयं नृपात्मज ॥","meaning":{"en":"How could I make you, the heir of the king of Matsya, born in a noble family and high-minded, do something disgraceful, prince?\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"एवमुक्तः स पार्थेन रथात्प्रस्कन्द्य कुण्डली ।\nआरुरोह शमीवृक्षं वैराटिरवशस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told so by Arjuna, Virata's son, wearing earrings, leapt down from the chariot and, helpless, climbed the shami tree."}},{"n":15,"text":"तमन्वशासच्छत्रुघ्नो रथे तिष्ठन्धनंजयः ।\nपरिवेष्टनमेतेषां क्षिप्रं चैव व्यपानुद ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya, killer of foes, standing in the chariot, instructed him: \"Quickly remove the wrappings from these.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"तथा संनहनान्येषां परिमुच्य समन्ततः ।\nअपश्यद्गाण्डिवं तत्र चतुर्भिरपरैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Untying their coverings all around, Uttara saw the Gandiva there with four other bows."}},{"n":17,"text":"तेषां विमुच्यमानानां धनुषामर्कवर्चसाम् ।\nविनिश्चेरुः प्रभा दिव्या ग्रहाणामुदयेष्विव ॥","meaning":{"en":"As those bows, shining like the sun, were unwrapped, a divine light came from them like planets rising."}},{"n":18,"text":"स तेषां रूपमालोक्य भोगिनामिव जृम्भताम् ।\nहृष्टरोमा भयोद्विग्नः क्षणेन समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing their forms like yawning serpents, his hair stood on end and in a moment he was shaken with fear."}},{"n":19,"text":"संस्पृश्य तानि चापानि भानुमन्ति बृहन्ति च ।\nवैराटिरर्जुनं राजन्निदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Touching those huge, radiant bows, Virata's son spoke these words to Arjuna, O king."}},{"text":"उत्तर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Uttara said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"बिन्दवो जातरूपस्य शतं यस्मिन्निपातिताः ।\nसहस्रकोटि सौवर्णाः कस्यैतद्धनुरुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Whose is this excellent bow on which a hundred gold bosses, a thousand crore of them, are fixed?"}},{"n":21,"text":"वारणा यस्य सौवर्णाः पृष्ठे भासन्ति दंशिताः ।\nसुपार्श्वं सुग्रहं चैव कस्यैतद्धनुरुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose is this excellent bow with golden elephants armored on its back, well shaped and well gripped?"}},{"n":22,"text":"तपनीयस्य शुद्धस्य षष्टिर्यस्येन्द्रगोपकाः ।\nपृष्ठे विभक्ताः शोभन्ते कस्यैतद्धनुरुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose is this excellent bow on whose back sixty gleaming pure-gold ladybirds are set in rows?"}},{"n":23,"text":"सूर्या यत्र च सौवर्णास्त्रयो भासन्ति दंशिताः ।\nतेजसा प्रज्वलन्तो हि कस्यैतद्धनुरुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose is this excellent bow with three golden suns shining, armored and blazing with splendor?"}},{"n":24,"text":"शालभा यत्र सौवर्णास्तपनीयविचित्रिताः ।\nसुवर्णमणिचित्रं च कस्यैतद्धनुरुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose is this excellent bow with golden locusts adorned with gold, painted with gold and gems?"}},{"n":25,"text":"इमे च कस्य नाराचाः सहस्रा लोमवाहिनः ।\nसमन्तात्कलधौताग्रा उपासङ्गे हिरण्मये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose are these thousands of iron arrows with hair-fine shafts, tipped with polished gold, in a golden quiver?"}},{"n":26,"text":"विपाठाः पृथवः कस्य गार्ध्रपत्राः शिलाशिताः ।\nहारिद्रवर्णाः सुनसाः पीताः सर्वायसाः शराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose are these broad vipatha arrows with vulture feathers, whetted on stone, turmeric-yellow, fine-nosed, yellow, wholly of iron?"}},{"n":27,"text":"कस्यायमसितावापः पञ्चशार्दूललक्षणः ।\nवराहकर्णव्यामिश्रः शरान्धारयते दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose is this black-covered quiver marked with five tigers, mixed with boar's ears, which holds ten arrows?"}},{"n":28,"text":"कस्येमे पृथवो दीर्घाः सर्वपारशवाः शराः ।\nशतानि सप्त तिष्ठन्ति नाराचा रुधिराशनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose are these broad, long arrows, all made of iron, seven hundred of them, blood-drinking nara-arrows?"}},{"n":29,"text":"कस्येमे शुकपत्राभैः पूर्वैरर्धैः सुवाससः ।\nउत्तरैरायसैः पीतैर्हेमपुङ्खैः शिलाशितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose are these, with parrot-feather look, fine-clothed in front half, iron and yellow behind, with gold feathers, stone-whetted?"}},{"n":30,"text":"कस्यायं सायको दीर्घः शिलीपृष्ठः शिलीमुखः ।\nवैयाघ्रकोशे निहितो हेमचित्रत्सरुर्महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose is this long arrow, with stone-ground back and tip, set in a tiger-skin sheath, with a golden-handled great one?"}},{"n":31,"text":"सुफलश्चित्रकोशश्च किङ्किणीसायको महान् ।\nकस्य हेमत्सरुर्दिव्यः खड्गः परमनिर्व्रणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose is this fine-headed arrow in a decorated sheath, a great bell-ringing arrow, and this divine sword with golden hilt, perfectly flawless?"}},{"n":32,"text":"कस्यायं विमलः खड्गो गव्ये कोशे समर्पितः ।\nहेमत्सरुरनाधृष्यो नैषध्यो भारसाधनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose is this spotless sword in a cowhide scabbard, with golden hilt, unassailable, from Nishadha, able to bear weight?"}},{"n":33,"text":"कस्य पाञ्चनखे कोशे सायको हेमविग्रहः ।\nप्रमाणरूपसंपन्नः पीत आकाशसंनिभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose is this arrow in a five-clawed sheath with a golden body, well proportioned, yellow like the sky?"}},{"n":34,"text":"कस्य हेममये कोशे सुतप्ते पावकप्रभे ।\nनिस्त्रिंशोऽयं गुरुः पीतः सैक्यः परमनिर्व्रणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose is this heavy yellow sword in a gold sheath, bright like fire when heated, hung on a strap and without a flaw?"}},{"n":35,"text":"निर्दिशस्व यथातत्त्वं मया पृष्टा बृहन्नडे ।\nविस्मयो मे परो जातो दृष्ट्वा सर्वमिदं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me truly what I have asked, Brihannada. I am greatly amazed at seeing all this wonder.\""}},{"text":"बृहन्नडोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brihannada said:"}},{"n":36,"text":"यन्मां पूर्वमिहापृच्छः शत्रुसेनानिबर्हणम् ।\nगाण्डीवमेतत्पार्थस्य लोकेषु विदितं धनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What you first asked me about, destroyer of enemy armies, is Partha's bow, known in the worlds as the Gandiva."}},{"n":37,"text":"सर्वायुधमहामात्रं शातकुम्भपरिष्कृतम् ।\nएतत्तदर्जुनस्यासीद्गाण्डीवं परमायुधम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is the chief of all weapons, adorned with gold; this was Arjuna's supreme weapon, the Gandiva."}},{"n":38,"text":"यत्तच्छतसहस्रेण संमितं राष्ट्रवर्धनम् ।\nयेन देवान्मनुष्यांश्च पार्थो विषहते मृधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"It equals a hundred thousand bows and makes kingdoms thrive; with it Partha withstands gods and men in battle."}},{"n":39,"text":"देवदानवगन्धर्वैः पूजितं शाश्वतीः समाः ।\nएतद्वर्षसहस्रं तु ब्रह्मा पूर्वमधारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Worshipped by gods, danavas and gandharvas for ages, Brahma carried it first for a thousand years."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततोऽनन्तरमेवाथ प्रजापतिरधारयत् ।\nत्रीणि पञ्चशतं चैव शक्रोऽशीति च पञ्च च ॥","meaning":{"en":"After that Prajapati carried it for three and five hundred years; Shakra for eighty-five;"}},{"n":41,"text":"सोमः पञ्चशतं राजा तथैव वरुणः शतम् ।\nपार्थः पञ्च च षष्टिं च वर्षाणि श्वेतवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Soma for five hundred, Varuna for a hundred, and Partha, the one with white horses, for sixty-five years."}},{"n":42,"text":"महावीर्यं महद्दिव्यमेतत्तद्धनुरुत्तमम् ।\nपूजितं सुरमर्त्येषु बिभर्ति परमं वपुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This mighty, great, divine and excellent bow, honored among gods and men, has a supreme form."}},{"n":43,"text":"सुपार्श्वं भीमसेनस्य जातरूपग्रहं धनुः ।\nयेन पार्थोऽजयत्कृत्स्नां दिशं प्राचीं परंतपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The bow with the fine sides and gold fittings belongs to Bhimasena, with which Partha, scorcher of foes, conquered the entire eastern quarter."}},{"n":44,"text":"इन्द्रगोपकचित्रं च यदेतच्चारुविग्रहम् ।\nराज्ञो युधिष्ठिरस्यैतद्वैराटे धनुरुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The beautiful bow marked with ladybirds is King Yudhishthira's, Virata's son, the excellent bow."}},{"n":45,"text":"सूर्या यस्मिंस्तु सौवर्णाः प्रभासन्ते प्रभासिनः ।\nतेजसा प्रज्वलन्तो वै नकुलस्यैतदायुधम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The one on which shining golden suns blaze with splendor is Nakula's weapon."}},{"n":46,"text":"शलभा यत्र सौवर्णास्तपनीयविचित्रिताः ।\nएतन्माद्रीसुतस्यापि सहदेवस्य कार्मुकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The one with golden locusts adorned with gold is the bow of Sahadeva, Madri's son."}},{"n":47,"text":"ये त्विमे क्षुरसंकाशाः सहस्रा लोमवाहिनः ।\nएतेऽर्जुनस्य वैराटे शराः सर्पविषोपमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The thousands of hair-fine razor-like arrows are Arjuna's, Virata's son, like the poison of snakes."}},{"n":48,"text":"एते ज्वलन्तः संग्रामे तेजसा शीघ्रगामिनः ।\nभवन्ति वीरस्याक्षय्या व्यूहतः समरे रिपून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Blazing in battle, quick and splendid, they never run out, and for the hero they break enemy ranks in war."}},{"n":49,"text":"ये चेमे पृथवो दीर्घाश्चन्द्रबिम्बार्धदर्शनाः ।\nएते भीमस्य निशिता रिपुक्षयकराः शराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The broad, long ones that look like half a moon are Bhima's sharp arrows that destroy foes."}},{"n":50,"text":"हारिद्रवर्णा ये त्वेते हेमपुङ्खाः शिलाशिताः ।\nनकुलस्य कलापोऽयं पञ्चशार्दूललक्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The turmeric-yellow, gold-feathered, stone-whetted arrows in the quiver marked with five tigers are Nakula's."}},{"n":51,"text":"येनासौ व्यजयत्कृत्स्नां प्रतीचीं दिशमाहवे ।\nकलापो ह्येष तस्यासीन्माद्रीपुत्रस्य धीमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With it that wise son of Madri conquered the entire western quarter in battle; this was his quiver."}},{"n":52,"text":"ये त्विमे भास्कराकाराः सर्वपारशवाः शराः ।\nएते चित्राः क्रियोपेताः सहदेवस्य धीमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sun-like arrows, all iron, various and skillfully made, are those of wise Sahadeva."}},{"n":53,"text":"ये त्विमे निशिताः पीताः पृथवो दीर्घवाससः ।\nहेमपुङ्खास्त्रिपर्वाणो राज्ञ एते महाशराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sharp, yellow, broad, long-clothed great arrows with gold feathers and three joints are the king's."}},{"n":54,"text":"यस्त्वयं सायको दीर्घः शिलीपृष्ठः शिलीमुखः ।\nअर्जुनस्यैष संग्रामे गुरुभारसहो दृढः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The long arrow with stone-ground back and tip is Arjuna's, firm and able to bear heavy strain in battle."}},{"n":55,"text":"वैयाघ्रकोशस्तु महान्भीमसेनस्य सायकः ।\nगुरुभारसहो दिव्यः शात्रवाणां भयंकरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great arrow in the tiger-skin sheath is Bhimasena's, divine, able to bear heavy burdens, terrifying to enemies."}},{"n":56,"text":"सुफलश्चित्रकोशश्च हेमत्सरुरनुत्तमः ।\nनिस्त्रिंशः कौरवस्यैष धर्मराजस्य धीमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fine-headed sword in the decorated sheath, with the best golden hilt, belongs to the Kaurava, wise King Dharmaraja."}},{"n":57,"text":"यस्तु पाञ्चनखे कोशे निहितश्चित्रसेवने ।\nनकुलस्यैष निस्त्रिंशो गुरुभारसहो दृढः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sword placed in the five-clawed sheath, decorated, is Nakula's, firm and able to bear weight."}},{"n":58,"text":"यस्त्वयं विमलः खड्गो गव्ये कोशे समर्पितः ।\nसहदेवस्य विद्ध्येनं सर्वभारसहं दृढम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And this spotless sword set in a cowhide scabbard, know it to be Sahadeva's, firm and able to bear any load.\""}}]}]}